# __NAME__

Game server scaffolded from the [moke-kit create-game](https://github.com/GStones/moke-kit) skill
(aligned with [moke-game/game](https://github.com/moke-game/game) secure defaults).

## Topology

| Entry | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `cmd/__NAME__/service` | Local aggregate: `AllModule` + `dfx.AuthModule` stub |
| `cmd/__NAME__/service-thin` | Game-only thin entry (swap stub for platform middleware) |
| TCP | Opt-in only (`AllWithTCPModule`) — **not** auth-protected |

For production-style split (game-only + remote platform auth), see moke-game/game
`cmd/game0/service-thin` and platform `AuthMiddlewareModule`. Swap the stub in
`main` — do not provide stub + platform auth together (duplicate `AuthMiddleware`).

## Run

```bash
cp .env.example .env   # if generated from .env.example.tmpl
docker compose -f ./deployment/docker-compose/infrastructure.yaml up -d
go run ./cmd/__NAME__/service/main.go
```

Public APIs require a bearer token. The stub treats the bearer as uid. Smoke:

```bash
curl -s -X POST localhost:8081/v1/hello/hi \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -H 'Authorization: bearer 10000' \
  -d '{"message":"hello","topic":"__NAME__"}'
```

Interactive client (default stub bearer `10000`; override with `__NAME__ token`):

```bash
go run ./cmd/__NAME__/client/main.go grpc
```

k6 smoke (stub by default; set `USE_PLATFORM_AUTH=1` + `AUTH_HOST` for platform Authenticate):

```bash
k6 run ./tests/__NAME__/__NAME__.js
```

